{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse serde::{Serialize, de::DeserializeOwned};\nuse habeas_sdk::graph::{CriterionPath, NodePath, Record};\n\n/// A directory of JSON records. Send + Sync; load/store futures are Send.\n/// Defined in habeas_sdk::storage.\npub struct FileEvidenceStorage { /* private fields */ }\n\npub enum FileStorageError {\n    Io(std::io::Error),\n    Json(serde_json::Error),\n}\n\nimpl FileEvidenceStorage {\n    /// Retain the root directory without performing filesystem I/O.\n    pub fn new(root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self;\n\n    /// Deserialize a record, or return None if its file is missing.\n    pub async fn load<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> Result<Option<Record<N, L>>, FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: DeserializeOwned + Send,\n        L: DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    /// Atomically replace this source/criterion pair's record.\n    pub async fn store<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<N, L>,\n    ) -> Result<(), FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: Serialize + Sync,\n        L: Serialize + Sync;\n}\n```\n\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type\nparameters do. `Criterion::Ok` is always serializable; its JSON value is\nalready in the record. Serialization bounds on node identities and edge labels\nbelong to this helper's use, rather than `Graph` itself.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs` adequately cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface`.\n\n- **`new` retains the root without filesystem I/O.**\n  - In `paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects`, the root is a directory that does not exist. After `new` and many `load` calls on missing records, it asserts `!root.exists()`. A `new` or `load` that created the root would fail this.\n  - `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` asserts `!root.exists()` after `new` and before the first `store`.\n- **`load` returns `None` when the file is missing.** `paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects` asserts `is_none()` for many node paths. `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` does the same for an unwritten node, and for a different node after another node's record was stored.\n- **`load` deserializes the stored record.** `records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error` stores a record and loads it back. It compares `revision`, `dependencies` and `output`. It covers both `Dependency::Node` and `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, with a `Fingerprint` and a string edge label. This also checks that `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` support Serde. The record's `output` is a JSON value, which matches the note that a `Criterion::Ok` value is already serialized in the record.\n- **`FileStorageError` has `Io` and `Json` variants.**\n  - Loading with the wrong node type parameter (`u8`) or the wrong edge label type parameter (`u8`) returns `Json`.\n  - Malformed file contents (`not JSON`) return `Json`.\n  - A directory at the record path returns `Io`.\n  - An over-long path component returns `Io` for both `load` and `store`.\n  - The tests also check that `to_string` matches the cause.\n- **`store` atomically replaces the record.** `concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes` has two writers repeatedly replace the record while a reader loads it. The reader asserts each record is a complete A or B record (8192-byte padding, matching revision and dependencies). It also asserts that the directory ends with exactly one entry, so no temp file is left behind. The `store` and nested-path tests check that `store` creates missing roots and parent directories.\n- **`Send + Sync` and `Send` futures.**\n  - The `send` helper in `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` requires the `load` and `store` futures to be `Send`. It is checked for the concrete `String` and `()` parameters.\n  - The concurrent test shares an `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` across scoped threads, which compiles only if the type is `Send + Sync`.\n- **Serialization bounds belong to the helper, not `Graph`.** `StoredGraph` in `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` implements `Graph` with `()` content and edge label. It delegates to the storage with a `String` node, with no serialization bounds on `Graph` itself.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests, and no obligation is left untested. There are no acknowledged gaps.",
